rter mile of Lawton Farm Lane."}, {"stage": 17, "statement": "the lower half mile of Harris Landing Road is flooded and impassable and the residence at the end of the road is flooded. Lenuds Ferry boat landing at Highway 41 is inaccessible and the parking lot is flooded."}, {"stage": 16, "statement": "water surrounds the residence at the end of Harris Landing Road and the adjacent boat ramp is inaccessible."}, {"stage": 12, "statement": "several dirt logging roads are impassable."}, {"stage": 10, "statement": "water covers numerous logging roads and inundates timber land adjacent to the river. Most access points to Wee Tee State Forest are cut off."}]}, "images": {"probability": {"weekint": {"stage": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/JAMS1.SSTG.prob.weekint.gif", "flow": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/JAMS1.QINE.prob.weekint.gif", "volume": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/JAMS1.volume.prob.weekint.gif"}, "entperiod": {"stage": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/JAMS1.SSTG.exceed.90day.gif", "flow": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/JAMS1.QINE.exceed.90day.gif", "volume": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/exceedance/JAMS1.volume.exceed.90day.gif"}, "shortrange": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/probabilistic/short_term/JAMS1.shortrange.hefs.png"}, "hydrograph": {"default": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/hydrographs/jams1_hg.png", "floodcat": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/hydrographs/jams1_record.png"}, "photos": [{"id": "7496216720067006958", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/7496216720067006958.jpeg", "caption": "View of gage on HWY 41 bridge from right bank of river. Stage at time of photo was 2.0 feet."}}, {"id": "7531802001583116782", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/7531802001583116782.jpeg", "caption": "View of gage on bridge from right bank. River was in minor flood at  11.3 feet."}}, {"id": "7537863269884629486", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/7537863269884629486.jpeg", "caption": "Downstream view of gage from right bank. River is at 2.0 feet."}}, {"id": "7544242756608070126", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/7544242756608070126.jpeg", "caption": "Upstream view from right bank. River is at 2.0 feet."}}, {"id": "7550610303322427886", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/7550610303322427886.jpeg", "caption": "Looking upstream toward boat ramp. River is in minor flood at 11.3 feet."}}, {"id": "7556026471831048686", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/7556026471831048686.jpeg", "caption": "Looking downstream while river is in minor flood at 11.3 feet."}}, {"id": "8212112769591284206", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/8212112769591284206.jpeg", "caption": "Record flooding during spring of 2003. Stage was around 24 feet at time of picture."}}, {"id": "8218206001039413742", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/8218206001039413742.jpeg", "caption": "Another view of record 2003 flooding."}}, {"id": "1621836730664554990", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/1621836730664554990.jpeg", "caption": "Flooded boat ramp on Highway 41 at stage 17.0 ft."}}, {"id": "6505949535380050414", "type": "Feature", "geometry": {"type": "Point", "coordinates": [33.3048893, -79.6781263]}, "properties": {"image": "https://water.noaa.gov/resources/photos/jams1/6505949535380050414.jpeg", "caption": "View downstream from Highway 41 bridge at stage 17.0 ft."}}]}, "dataAttribution": [{"abbrev": "USGS", "text": "02171700", "title": "Observations courtesy of U.S. Geological Survey", "url": "https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02171700/#dataTypeId=continuous-00065-0&period=P7D"}], "impactsLowWaters": [], "normalThreshold": null, "hydronotes": [{"statement": "River forecasts for this location take into account past precipitation and the precipitation amounts expected approximately 48 hours into the future from the forecast issuance time.", "effective": "0101", "expiration": "1231"}], "datums": {"vertical": {"value": [{"label": "North American Vertical Datum of 1988", "abbrev": "NAVD88", "description": "A fixed reference for elevations determined by geodetic leveling. The datum was derived from a general adjustment of the first-order terrestrial leveling nets of the United States, Canada, and Mexico. In the adjustment, only the height of the primary tidal bench mark, referenced to the International Great Lakes Datum of 1985 (IGLD 85) local mean sea level height value, at Father Point, Rimouski, Quebec, Canada was held fixed, thus providing minimum constraint. NAVD 88 and IGLD 85 are identical. However, NAVD 88 bench mark values are given in Helmert orthometric height units while IGLD 85 values are in dynamic heights. See International Great Lakes Datum of 1985, National Geodetic Vertical Datum of 1929, and geopotential difference. NAVD 88 should not be used as Mean Sea Level.", "value": -0.86}, {"label": "National Geodetic Vertical Datum of 1929", "abbrev": "NGVD29", "description": "A fixed reference adopted as a standard geodetic datum for elevations determined by leveling. The datum was derived for surveys from a general adjustment of the first-order leveling nets of both the United States and Canada. In the adjustment, mean sea level was held fixed as observed at 21 tide stations in the United States and 5 in Canada. The year indicates the time of the general adjustment. A synonym for Sea-level Datum of 1929. The geodetic datum is fixed and does not take into account the changing stands of sea level. Because there are many variables affecting sea level, and because the geodetic datum represents a best fit over a broad area, the relationship between the geodetic datum and local mean sea level is not consistent from one location to another in either time or space. For this reason, the National Geodetic Vertical Datum should not be confused with mean sea level. See North American Vertical Datum of 1988 (NAVD 88). NGVD 29 should not be used as Mean Sea Level. NGVD 29 is no longer supported by NGS.", "value": 0.13}]}, "horizontal": {"value": []}, "notes": {"value": []}}, "inundation": {"enabled": false, "url": "", "zeroDatum": null, "downloads": null, "siteSpecificInfo": "", "dataAttribution": []}, "upstreamLid": "SNRS1", "downstreamLid": "SSNS1", "inService": {"enabled": true, "message": ""}, "lowThreshold": null, "forecastReliability": "Forecasts are issued as needed during times of high water, but are not routinely available.", "TruncateObs": "-1", "TruncateFcst": "5", "ObservedFloodCategory": "no_flooding", "ForecastFloodCategory": "fcst_not_current"}